ons of the quantum groups as Markov matrices. A Markov matrix must satisfy the positivity of non-diagonal elements and the zero-sum rule for each column. Therefore, the higher-dimensional representations constructed from the fusion rule cannot be used as a Markov matrix. We construct a matrix equipped with the two requirements above by decomposing the fused matrix in a proper way. (https://www.ms.u-tokyo.ac.jp/activity/documents/AnnualReport2019.pdf)\nciteturn1search17 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.9 years ago; A Markov matrix must satisfy the positivity of non-diagonal elements and the zero-sum rule for each column. ... We construct a matrix equipped with the two requirements above by decomposing the fused matrix in a proper way. ... Matsui: “Multi-state asymmetric simple exclusion processes”, J.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA Unified Approach to Unimodality of Gaussian Polynomials (https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/1994673)\nciteturn1search18 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.5 years ago; Crawled: 3.2 years ago; *The Theory of Partitions*. ... An overpartition analogue of q-binomial coefficients, II: Combinatorial proofs and \\((q,t)\\)-log concavity. ... Restricted k-color partitions, II. ... A generalization of a 1998 unimodality conjecture of Reiner and Stanton.\n"
